From 087e2a70795927926a5b2dabccd5e7f8900821db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:04:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 61/61] PERF-104: shader precompilation removed

Lance asked for shader precompilation to be deleted completely (renderer
and launcher). Removed from the renderer:

- PERF-098: the GPU.precompile_shaders setting, the splash-screen progress
  bar, and the command thread's idle pipeline builds while the splash shows.
- PERF-102: the guest clock hold while the precompile runs, and the splash
  screen waiting for it.
- PERF-038: background builds of stored pipelines (reader thread,
  IdlePrewarm/InstallPrewarmed, the build queue's background/boost/pause
  modes, SHADGT_PREWARM, perf id 52, GraphicsPipeline's preloading build),
  and the stored pipeline records only they read: pipeline keys are no longer
  written to the store (RegisterPipelineData, LoadStoredGraphicsPipeline,
  PeekShaderMeta, DataBase::ListBlobs).
- PB-1 to PB-4: the shader pack rebuild (RebuildFromPrograms, ReplayTranslate),
  the recompiler's replay hooks (t_replay/ReplayInputs), and the research
  tools SHADGT_REPLAY_TEST, SHADGT_TEMPLATE_TEST, SHADGT_DUMP_STORE and
  RYGT_SCAN_READS.
- ryty_hle_precompile.cpp is now ryty_hle_overlay_stub.cpp (only the
  controller overlay stub is left).

Kept: PERF-032's shader store (this PC's own translations, loaded on first
use), PERF-076/PERF-103 compile modes and FIX-044's clock pause, which handle
compiles at run time. Comments describing the removed feature are reworded;
GT_SPORT_OPTIMIZATION_LOG.md gets a PERF-104 entry. test_build_queue.cpp
follows the simpler queue.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
